hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2923","Harith al-Awur narrated that the issue of Banu Umm was brought to Sayyiduna Ali, one of whom was his maternal brother, and Sayyiduna Ali was told that Sayyiduna Ibn Masud, Radiallahu Anhu, had made him the heir of all wealth."
"2924","Hazeel bin Shahrabeel said: A man came to Abu Musa Ash'ari and Salman bin Rabi'ah and asked them both about the share of the inheritance of the daughter, granddaughter and real sister, so they both said: The daughter will get half and the rest is for the sister (because the presence of the daughter is a hindrance for the granddaughter). He went and asked for a fatwa about this, and he said: If I give such a fatwa, I will be misled and will not be among the guided people."
"2925","It was narrated from Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, said about real sisters and half-sisters: two-thirds will be for real sisters, and what remains will be for men only, not for women. Then when Masrooq came to Medina, he heard the words of Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him. He replied that when I came to Madinah, I found Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, among the strong and firm scholars. \n Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus said: I asked Ibn Shihab: What did Sayyiduna Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu say about this? So he said that he made all the real and the patriarchs partners."
"2926","Ismail bin Abi Khalid said: We mentioned to Hakeem bin Jabir that Sayyidna Ibn Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) gives two-thirds of the inheritance to real sisters and paternal brothers and sisters, and what is left over they divide only among men and do not give anything to women."
"2927","It was narrated from Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, that: Sayyida Aisha used to share the inheritance with two daughters, one granddaughter and one grandson, so she used to give two thirds to the two daughters and share the remaining one third with everyone. \n And Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) did not share the granddaughter, he used to divide what was left among the men only, and he used to say: Sisters are on the same level as daughters."
"2928","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud, may God be pleased with him, used to say about a daughter, several granddaughters, and a grandson, that even if they received less than six hundred in the distribution, they would give them six hundred, and if it came more than six hundred, then they would give them six hundred. \n Daughter half 3 \n Grandson Sahman 2 \n Granddaughter Saham Sudas"
"2929","It was narrated on the authority of Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, that he used to share the inheritance with his daughter, granddaughter, and two sisters, so Alqamah said to him, \"Among those who said this, was there anyone more knowledgeable than Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him)?\" Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, said: No, but I saw Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, and the people of Madinah, that he used to associate with them."
"2930","Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, narrated from Qazi Shareeh that if a woman left her husband, mother, real sister, paternal sister and maternal brother, then they divided it by six and increased it to ten, and gave three shares (i.e. three out of six) to the husband and half of it, then gave the remaining three shares (one half share) to the real sister, then gave six (one share) to the mother and one third (two shares) to the maternal brothers and one share to the paternal sister completing three thirds."
"2931","Shaabi said that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) did not deprive any heir because of infidels and slaves, and did not make infidels and slaves inherit anything. And Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to deprive them because of the infidels and Mamluks, but did not give them inheritance."
"2932","Ibrahim said: Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) said: The Mamluks and the People of the Book will neither deprive nor inherit, and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with them) said: They will deprive but not inherit."
"2933","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote about the inheritance of his grandfather, but when he was wounded by a spear, he called for the writing and erased it and said: You people use your own opinion about this."
"2934","Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: I said to Ubaydah: Tell me about Dada. He replied that I remember eighty different issues about Dada."
"2935","Abdullah bin Amr Kharfi said: A man came to Sayyiduna Ali and asked about the duty (of inheritance), so he said: If grandfather is not mentioned in it, then ask."
"2936","A man of Murad heard Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) saying: He who likes to enter the germs of hell should decide in the matter of grandfather and brothers."
"2937","Abu Nazra narrated from Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) and Ikrima narrated from Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) that he placed Dada in the rank of father."
"2938","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) that Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) gave grandfather the status of father."
"2939","From this chain of narrators, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the same as before."
"2940","Sayyidna Uthman bin Affan (RA) has also narrated the same from Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA)."
"2941","Also from this chain of narrators, it is narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) that Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) used to give grandfather the status of father."
"2942","Abu Barda said: I met Marwan bin Al-Hikam in Madinah, and he said: O son of Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may God be pleased with him! Shall I not inform you that grandfather is not in the status of father to you and you do not even deny it? Abu Burda said: I said: You do not do that either. Marwan replied: I bear witness that Sayyidna Uthman (RA) testified that Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) placed grandfather in the position of father in his father's absence."
"2943","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) used to give grandfather the status of father."
"2944","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: About whom the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If I were to make someone a friend, I would make him (i.e. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) a friend, but Islamic brotherhood (brotherhood) is more preferable.\" He said grandfather is like father."
"2945","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) said: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) gave grandfather the status of father."
"2946","Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: The Sunnah has been passed down about Dada that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) gave Dada the status of father, but (today) people have taken a different opinion."
"2947","Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The first in Islam is Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) who took inheritance as a grandfather."
"2948","Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the first grandfather who inherited his share. Sayyidna Ali and Zayd, may God be pleased with him, came to him and said, \"No, you are like two brothers.\""
"2949","Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyiduna Umar used to share the distribution with one or two brothers."
"2950","It was narrated from Marwan bin Al-Hikam that when Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) was wounded by a spear, he consulted the Companions about Dada and said, \"I had an opinion about Dada, if you want, follow it.\""
"2951","When Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) was in Basra, he wrote to Sayyidna Ali (RA) that I have been asked about the issue of grandfather and six brothers. \n (That is, the rest of the Khamsa for Sadas Dada is for Asadas brothers)."
"2952","Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated about the legacy of six brothers and grandfather that he should give one-sixth (sixth) to grandfather. \n Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: That is, Shaabi used to narrate the sayings of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2953","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Salama (al-Maradi) that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to list the grandfather as a brother, even though he was the sixth person."
"2954","It was narrated from Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to share the grandfather with his brothers and give them one-sixth."
"2955","Abdullah Bin Salamah (Al-Maradi) said: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to share the inheritance with the grandfather and the brothers until the grandfather was the sixth person."
"2956","Ibrahim said: Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to make six brothers with the grandfather and give each one a share, and with the grandfather he would not give anything from the inheritance to the maternal brother and sister, and with the children he would not give more than sixty percent of the grandfather's share unless it was someone other than the son. They used to divide it half and half between them, and if there were brothers and sisters among the heirs, they used to share the grandfather with the sadas (sixth part)."
"2957","Abd al-Rahman bin Muaqal said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, was asked about his grandfather, and he said: Who is the greatest of your fathers (grandfathers)? (And in the narration: When the questioner did not answer) I said: Adam (is the greatest father) He replied: You have not heard the word of Allah, \"O children of Adam.\""
"2958","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I wish (about Dada) that I and those who oppose me should curse each other who says something wrong (i.e. curse him who says something wrong)."
"2959","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas Radiyallahu Anhu called Dada as father."
"2960","Abu Ishaq said: I entered Shareih with the problem of the inheritance of one of my women, Aaliyah, and Amir, Ibrahim, Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah were sitting near him. This woman left her husband, her mother, and her paternal brother and grandfather. I said: No, so they said: Half for the husband, a third for the mother. I waited for them to give me another answer, but when they did not give me any answer other than that, Ibrahim, Amir and Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah said: No one came with such a difficult problem as you have come with a difficult problem. There is no one who knows the duties more than Ubaydah. He used to sit in the mosque and when (the judge) Shareeh had an inheritance problem in which the grandfather was present, he would hand it over to Ubaydah. So I asked him, and he said: If you want, I will recite the decision of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, on this matter. share (Sudas), gave one share to brother and one share to grandfather."
